@page "/overview-detail"
@rendermode InteractiveServer
@using Microsoft.JSInterop
@implements IAsyncDisposable
@inject IJSRuntime JS

<PageTitle>Overview and detail — GGNet Demo</PageTitle>

<h1 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Overview and detail</h1>

<p class="mt-2 max-w-prose text-gray-600">
    The page owns which chart is open; GGNet supplies the pieces. Tap a
    sub-panel to open it: the temperature panel has a detail chart with an
    extra equipment-activity panel. The time window travels with you in both
    directions, and only the Close button returns to the overview. Both
    charts stay mounted; the hidden one ignores input.
</p>

<div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-6 gap-y-2 text-sm">
    <span>Showing <b data-qa="state">@(open ? "detail" : "overview")</b></span>
    <span>Activations <b data-qa="activations" class="text-lg">@activations</b></span>
    <span>Last activation <b data-qa="last-activation">@lastActivation</b></span>
    <button class="rounded-md border border-gray-300 bg-white px-3 py-1.5 text-sm hover:bg-gray-100" data-qa="close" disabled=@(!open) @onclick=CloseAsync>Close detail</button>
</div>

<div class="mt-2 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-6 gap-y-1 font-mono text-xs text-gray-600">
    <span>overview window <b data-qa="overview-window">@Format(overviewWindow)</b></span>
    <span>changes <b data-qa="overview-changes">@overviewChanges</b></span>
    <span>cause <b data-qa="overview-cause">@overviewCause</b></span>
</div>

<div class="mt-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-6 gap-y-1 font-mono text-xs text-gray-600">
    <span>detail window <b data-qa="detail-window">@Format(detailWindow)</b></span>
    <span>changes <b data-qa="detail-changes">@detailChanges</b></span>
    <span>cause <b data-qa="detail-cause">@detailCause</b></span>
</div>

<div class="mt-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 bg-white p-4 shadow-sm" style="position: relative;">
    <div data-qa="overview" style=@Layer(!open)>
        <Plot T="TelemetryReading" TX="Instant" TY="double" @ref=overview Context=@overviewContext RenderMode=@renderMode Interactivity=@navigate ViewChanged=@OnOverviewViewChanged />
    </div>
    <div data-qa="detail" style=@($"position: absolute; inset: 1rem; {Layer(open)}")>
        <Plot T="TelemetryReading" TX="Instant" TY="double" @ref=detail Context=@detailContext RenderMode=@renderMode Interactivity=@navigate ViewChanged=@OnDetailViewChanged />
    </div>
</div>

<h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold">Cost of the hidden chart</h2>

<p class="mt-2 max-w-prose text-gray-600">
    Both charts read the same readings, and a live page refreshes both when
    one arrives. Measure with the overview showing: the last reading changes
    twenty times with only the overview refreshed, then twenty times with the
    hidden detail refreshed too. Each time runs from the request to the frame
    after the new drawing is on screen.
</p>

<div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-6 gap-y-2 text-sm">
    <button class="rounded-md border border-gray-300 bg-white px-3 py-1.5 text-sm hover:bg-gray-100" data-qa="measure" disabled=@(open || measuring) @onclick=MeasureAsync>Measure refresh</button>
    <span class="font-mono text-xs" data-qa="measure-result">@measurement</span>
</div>

<h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold">Activation without gestures</h2>

<p class="mt-2 max-w-prose text-gray-600">
    This chart sets no interactivity, so a tap anywhere in the plot area
    (a mark, a grid line or the background) activates at once.
</p>

<div class="mt-3 text-sm">
    <span>Activations <b data-qa="plain-activations" class="text-lg">@plainActivations</b></span>
</div>

<div data-qa="plain" class="mt-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 bg-white p-4 shadow-sm">
    <Plot Context=@plainContext RenderMode=@renderMode />
</div>

<h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold">Activation against inspection</h2>

<p class="mt-2 max-w-prose text-gray-600">
    With the crosshair and cursor tooltip on, a tap inspects and never
    activates: the counter stays at zero. A page that wants both gives the
    user its own control, like the button here.
</p>

<div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-6 gap-y-2 text-sm">
    <span>Activations <b data-qa="inspect-activations" class="text-lg">@inspectActivations</b></span>
    <span>Button presses <b data-qa="inspect-opens" class="text-lg">@inspectOpens</b></span>
    <button class="rounded-md border border-gray-300 bg-white px-3 py-1.5 text-sm hover:bg-gray-100" data-qa="inspect-open" @onclick=@(() => inspectOpens++)>Open</button>
</div>

<div data-qa="inspect" class="mt-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 bg-white p-4 shadow-sm">
    <Plot Context=@inspectContext RenderMode=@renderMode Interactivity=@inspect />
</div>
